{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>May YHWH bless you and guard you</b> — the initial letters of the words total 26, corresponding to the Name of four letters, and the final letters כה\"ך total 45, corresponding to the Name of מ\"ה, and this is (Psalm 121:8) 'YHWH will guard your going out and your coming in.' And three words in the verse, to recall the merit of three patriarchs, and in them 15 letters, after the manner of the patriarchs who saw one another, all three together, 15 years, and the merit of the tribes together with the patriarchs is 15. 'May He bless you' — in the merit of Abraham, concerning whom it is written (Genesis 24:1) 'And YHWH had blessed Abraham in all,' and three words in that verse, corresponding to three blessings stated concerning him: 'And I will bless you' (Genesis 12:2), 'And you shall be a blessing' (Genesis 12:2), 'And I will bless those who bless you' (Genesis 12:3)." "<b>May YHWH bless you</b> — in gematria: בנכסים ובגוף (in property and in body)."], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {0 "The phrase כה\"ך appears to denote the final letters of the three words יברכך יהוה וישמרך, which are ך-ה-ך; the notation is unusual and may reflect a variant or abbreviated form."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:21:20.229773719Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}